  "notes": "{味見|あじみ} means tasting food to check its flavor, especially while cooking. Compound of {味|あじ} (taste) + {見|み} (checking).\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- Xの{味見|あじみ}をする: to taste X\n- {味見|あじみ}してみる: to try tasting\n- {味見|あじみ}してから{塩|しお}を{足|た}す: to taste before adding salt\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {試食|ししょく}: food tasting/sampling (at a store, not while cooking)\n- {試飲|しいん}: drink tasting/sampling\n- {味|あじ}をみる: to check the taste (synonym)\n{味見|あじみ} is typically done by the cook during preparation, while {試食|ししょく} refers to free samples offered at shops or events.",
